/-!
# The binary long-A2 Levi in the original F4 coordinates

The four literal signed long-root generators give a faithful representation
of SL3(2) on the existing 52-dimensional coordinate space. A common pool of
141 binary rows certifies multiplication by each generator for the 168
matrices. Generator words prove surjectivity onto the subgroup A; restriction
to coordinates 6, 8 and 10 proves injectivity. Only the resulting equivalence
is public. All finite certificates are checked by the Lean kernel.

The root matrices and ordering are the integral Geck coordinates described
in `BinaryCoordinates` and `A02ParabolicSections.SourceLevi.F4` (GLS3 1.12,
2.6). This identifies the actual carrier used in the original-action test
for Aschbacher--Smith C.1.34, printed pp.136--137, and the F4 example in
Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher (1993), printed p.831.
-/

